.TH NETWORK-CONFIG 4 "31 October 2026" "amix-base"
.SH NAME
network-config, rc.inet \- network commands run at every boot
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /etc/inet/network-config
.br
.B /etc/inet/rc.inet
.SH DESCRIPTION
Both files are run by
.B /etc/init.d/inetinit
at every boot, as root:
.B network-config
is read by the shell after
.B "ifup \-a"
has been started in the background, and
.B rc.inet
is run last.
.PP
They are kept, empty, for instructions written for the stock system, such
as \(lqadd this line to network-config\(rq.
The interfaces themselves, their addresses, the default route and DNS come
from
.BR /etc/inet/interfaces ;
nothing needs to be written here for them.
Because the interfaces come up in the background, a line here may run
before an interface is up.
.PP
An update of the base package keeps either file when it has been edited,
and puts the new default beside it as
.IB file .new\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ifup (1M),
.BR interfaces (4)
